            <description>Solar occultation time series.
                Each record (row) in the table corresponds to one integration period of either
                1, 2, 4, 5.5, or 37 seconds depending on the occultation observed.
                
                The Sun is an extended source and therefore its projected position onto the ring plane
                changes over the course of an integration period. We provide the start of an integration
                period, middle of an integration period, and end of an integration period times and the
                corresponding ring plane radial values in case future analyses would require knowledge
                of the change of the Sun's position over an integration period. The order of the time specific columns is mid integration, start integration, stop integration.
            </description>
