                        equals 90 degrees along the right ansa and 270 degrees along the left ansa. Values range from 0 to 360 degrees.
                               </description>
                </Field_Character>
                <Field_Character>
                    <name>Ring Longitude</name>
                    <field_number>11</field_number>
                    <field_location unit="byte">157</field_location>
                    <data_type>ASCII_Real</data_type>
                    <field_length unit="byte">10</field_length>
                    <unit>deg</unit>
                    <description>Ring Longitude specifies the inertial longitude of a ring feature relative to the prime
                        meridian. In planetary ring systems, the prime meridian is the ascending node of the planet's invariable
                        plane on the Earth's mean equator of J2000. Longitudes are measured in the direction of orbital motion
                        along the planet's invariable plane to the ring's ascending node, and thence along the ring plane. Values
                        range from 0 to 360 in units of degrees. Note: The invariable plane of a planet is equivalent to its
                        equatorial plane for every ringed planet except Neptune.
                        NOTE: This simplifies to the inertial (J2000) longitude, in the ring plane, of the ring-plane intercept point
                        at the ring [start, midpoint, or stop] event time because the planet’s equator plane and the ring plane are the
                        same plane.
                               </description>
                </Field_Character>
                <Field_Character>
                    <name>Spacecraft To Ring Intercept Distance</name>
                    <field_number>12</field_number>
                    <field_location unit="byte">169</field_location>
                    <data_type>ASCII_Real</data_type>
                    <field_length unit="byte">11</field_length>
                    <unit>km</unit>
                    <description>The distance between the spacecraft (at the Observed Event Time) and the ring-plane intercept
                        point (at the Ring Event Time).
                        NOTE: When multiple values are given for an "Event Time" (e.g., both ring_event_TDB_start_integration and
                        ring_event_TDB_stop_integration are given), the description in the label for Spacecraft To Ring Intercept
                        Distance must specify which "Event Time" is referenced.
                               </description>
                </Field_Character>
                <Field_Character>
                    <name>Projected Sun Diameter</name>
                    <field_number>13</field_number>
                    <field_location unit="byte">182</field_location>
                    <data_type>ASCII_Real</data_type>
                    <field_length unit="byte">8</field_length>
                    <unit>kilometer</unit>
                    <description>The diameter in kilometers of the sun projected onto
                                   the ring plane radius based on the line of sight from the observer
                                   to the ring plane at the start of the integration assuming that at
                                   the orbit of Saturn the sun subtends a circular disk with an
                                   angular size of 1 mrad.
                                </description>
                </Field_Character>
                <Field_Character>
                    <name>Raw Total Counts</name>
                    <field_number>14</field_number>
